message: "If you use Open Bitcoin Metrics (OBM), please cite both the archived dataset release and the accompanying manuscript."
title: "Open Bitcoin Metrics (OBM): Reproducible Full-Node Bitcoin On-Chain Time Series"
version: "v0.1.0"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Llanos"
    given-names: "Diego R."
    affiliation: "University of Valladolid"
    email: "diego.llanos@uva.es"
repository-code: "https://github.com/diegorllanos/open-bitcoin-metrics"
url: "https://github.com/diegorllanos/open-bitcoin-metrics"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21156871"
date-released: "2026-07-03"
abstract: >-
  Open Bitcoin Metrics (OBM) is a reproducible, full-node-derived dataset
  and reference guide for Bitcoin on-chain time series designed for economic
  and econometric research. The dataset provides documented daily series
  covering block production, block-space usage, transaction counts, supply,
  issuance, fees, miner revenue, mining difficulty, estimated hashrate,
  Bitcoin Days Destroyed, dormancy, liveliness, UTXO counts, spent output
  value, and related UTXO-age indicators. Metrics are reconstructed from a
  locally maintained Bitcoin Core full node, a persistent spent-output indexer,
  or deterministic transformations of previously generated OBM series.
keywords:
  - Bitcoin
  - on-chain data
  - time series
  - Bitcoin full node
  - reproducibility
  - econometrics
  - open data
